// Aim down sights (auf::aim_down_sights): the left trigger raises the gun to the middle of the view and zooms in a
// little, as in a PC shooter, instead of the game's manual aim (the view held still, a crosshair moved by the stick).
//
// The player (thiscall objects) keeps its command at +0x648: the buttons at +0x64C, last frame's at +0x4D8, the released
// ones at +0x660. Its input handler 0xBB990 sets manual aim (+0x671) while bit 0x1000 (the left trigger) is held; that
// byte sets the turn rates (0xB45C0), stops walking (0xB46E0) and moves the crosshair. For a gun without a scope the bit
// is taken from the three words before the handler runs, so manual aim never starts: the view turns, Bond walks and
// shots go through the middle. A scoped gun's zoom entry (its weapon's vfunc +0x170, 0xA08E0 "tozoom") differs from the
// plain guns' 0xAE770, which keeps the game's scope. The weapon is [player+0x2EC]; the fists (vtable 0x1E5FC8) are left
// alone too.
// While aiming, eased in and out over kEase:
// - the zoom: 0xB55C0 (thiscall player, the field of view a float at [esp+4]) takes it divided by up to kZoom
// - the gun: 0x27C40 (eax the local player, ecx its view model's offset, x across, y up, z ahead, before 0x27D90
//   negates it) has its x drawn to kSightX and kSightY added: the sights in the middle
// - the crosshair: 0x51320 (cdecl, [esp+8] the player) is skipped; the Q-camera's (mode 0x107 at the HUD state
//   0x2F6AC0 + i*0x19C, +0x158) still draws
// Weapon sway (auf::weapon_sway), in the same offset: the gun trails the view's turn (the angles 0x2A8124 pitch and
// 0x2A8128 yaw, 0x30 a player, degrees) a little and settles back, less while aiming.
// AUF_ADS_TRACE=1 logs aiming's start and end.
//
// The sight tuner (auf::sight_tuner, debug, off by default), from NightFire's: each gun's own correction of kSight, kept
// by its class name (the ClassDef's +0 through the vtable's first function, "mov eax, def; ret": "P2K", "KA57", ...) in
// sight_offsets.txt beside the exe, a line a gun: "name right up farther turn tilt roll" (offset units as the screen
// shows them, degrees), added to the gun's offset and angles while aiming. Read at the first aim, applied always. While
// tuning, player 1 aims all the time without sway or bob and is given every single-player gun whose model the level has
// loaded (each level's maps\<name>.xbc holds only its own; GiveGuns), with ammo. NightFire's keys: comma and full stop
// pick the gun (Q too), the arrows move it, Home/End nearer/farther, J L turn, I K tilt, U O roll, Shift finer; Enter
// saves every gun's correction, Delete resets the held one. src/common/sight_tuner.cpp draws the panel and the true
// centre and holds those keys back from the game.
